  "rationale": "Dolphy's third album, co-led with trumpeter Booker Little, is a defining post-bop statement that bridges the hard bop tradition with the emerging avant-garde. The Penguin Guide to Jazz awards it a core 4-star rating, AllMusic 4.5 stars, and Rolling Stone's Jazz Record Guide 5 stars. Features the first recorded appearance of Dolphy's celebrated composition 'Miss Ann' and a landmark unaccompanied alto solo on 'Tenderly' that anticipates Anthony Braxton's solo work. The ensemble of Dolphy, Booker Little, Jaki Byard, Ron Carter, and Roy Haynes represents a peak gathering of the era's forward-looking musicians. Consensus across Penguin Guide, AllMusic, Rolling Stone, and DownBeat (3.5 stars).",
