    "tier": "consensus_core",
    "priority": "strong",
    "case_for": "This is a load-bearing early post-bop bridge: Dolphy's radical alto, flute, and bass-clarinet language remains grounded in Parker tributes, standards, blues, and hard-bop ensemble practice (S1, S2). The session's personnel\u2014Jaki Byard, Ron Carter, and Roy Haynes, with Booker Little on \"Miss Ann\"\u2014has exceptional session gravity. Cross-reference support from Penguin, AllMusic, Rolling Stone, and DownBeat (S2).",
    "case_against": "Far Cry is an important transitional date rather than Dolphy's most definitive album; Out to Lunch! is the more urgent single statement. Little's appearance on only one track makes the co-led framing somewhat overstated.",
    "disagreement": null,
    "recommendation": "The council proposes that John treat Far Cry as a strong, consensus-core inclusion.",
